  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How does a chick breathe inside an egg?",
      "a": "Oxygen passes in through thousands of tiny pores in the shell and is picked up by a membrane full of blood vessels lining the inside, which works like a lung. Just before hatching, the chick starts breathing air from the air cell.",
      "asks": [
        "Can a chick breathe in its shell?",
        "How does air get into an egg?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": "How does a chick get out of its egg?",
      "a": "The chick breaks through using its egg tooth, a hard point on the tip of its beak, and a strong hatching muscle in its neck. It chips a ring around the shell and pushes the top off. The egg tooth falls off soon after.",
      "asks": [
        "What is an egg tooth?",
        "How do chicks hatch?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": "Why does an egg need to be kept warm?",
      "a": "The chick grows only at about 37 to 38 degrees Celsius. The hen sits on her eggs to warm them with a bare patch of skin, and turns them several times a day so the embryo does not stick to the shell membranes.",
      "asks": [
        "Why do hens sit on eggs?",
        "What temperature does an egg need?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": "What is the yolk for?",
      "a": "The yolk is the chick's food store, rich in fat and protein. Just before hatching, the last of the yolk is drawn into the chick's belly, feeding it for its first day or two.",
      "asks": [
        "Is the yolk the baby chick?",
        "What does the chick eat inside the egg?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": "How long does a chick take to hatch?",
      "a": "A chicken egg takes about 21 days to hatch once it is kept warm. Ducks take about 28 days, and some big birds, like albatrosses, take over two months.",
      "asks": [
        "How many days until an egg hatches?",
        "Do all eggs take the same time to hatch?"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "facts": [
    "A chicken egg takes about 21 days to hatch.",
